        "orario": "16:09",
        "timestamp": 1780150197,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Live PSG vs Arsenal live: follow the Champions League final Sport Issued on: 30/05/2026 - 16:09 Modified: 30/05/2026 - 16:53 Paris Saint-Germain and Arsenal face off in the Champions League final in Budapest on Saturday, with the biggest prize in European club football up for grabs. Title holders PSG can become only the second team in the modern era to retain the trophy, but Arsenal head into the game on a fresh high after lifting the Premier League title for the first time in 22 years. Follow the match on our liveblog, kickoff is at 6pm local time (GMT+2). 30/05/2026 - 16:53 Free-scoring attack vs clean sheet machine The final has been billed as a tussle between the 'unstoppable force' of PSG's attack Arsenal's 'immovable object' in defence. The Gunners have conceded just six goals in the tournament, staying unbeaten, and goalkeeper David Raya has a staggering nine clean sheets, matching the all-time record. In front of him Gabriel and William Saliba form a formidable centre-back pairing for Ballon d'Or winner Ousmane Dembélé to try and break through, supported by Georgian wizzard Khvicha Kvaratskhelia and the ever smooth Désiré Doué. PSG have ammassed 44 goals in the tournament, just one short of the record of 45 set by Barcelona in the 1999-2000 campaign. 30/05/2026 - 16:45 Festive mood as fans gather at the Puskas Arena Fans of the French and English champions are gathering at the stadium in Budapest, where pre-match entertainment is being provided by American rock band The Killers. Selina Sykes and Karim Baldé bring us the latest. 30/05/2026 - 16:37 30/05/2026 - 16:37 Welcome to our liveblog Title holders Paris Saint-Germain face Arsenal in the Champions League final at the Puskas Arena, seeking to cement their status among Europe’s elite a year after finally lifting the trophy they have craved for so long. Twelve months on from their trouncing of Inter Milan, PSG's hunger has not faded, with captain Marquinhos and coach Luis Enrique insisting the club’s historic breakthrough only sharpened their appetite for more silverware. But Arsenal ⁠are equally hungry ​to write history and join the select club of Champions League winners, fresh from clinching the Premier League title that had eluded them for 22 years. Kickoff is in just over 90 minutes. 30/05/2026 - 16:31 30/05/2026 - 15:32 Paris Saint-Germain's irresistible attacking force prepares to collide with the defensive steel of Arsenal in the UEFA Champions League final, in an intriguing clash of opposing styles at the Puskas Arena in Budapest. PSG coach Luis Enrique said that there were \"no favourites\" going into the European showpiece against Mikel Arteta's Premier League champions, and insisted that the devil will be \"in the details\". While the bookmakers do classify the Ligue 1 winners and current Champions League holders as favourites , they also suggest that this is the hardest final to call since 2018, when Real Madrid beat Liverpool."
